Informal statement: if a replacement value occurs at an index in the first
modification set, then a nearby replacement value occurs at the same index in
the second modification set.

Lean strategy / thesis relation note: the theorem uses the thesis' radius restriction `r ≤ 1`, which
is what forces the matching point in the Hausdorff comparison to have the same
natural-number index.
